v0.11.3: orchestra follow-ups — admin inbox, manager-effect substrate, live roster

Three items requested after v0.11.2 (orchestra registry) that all
answer the same practical question: Mario successfully published
`guidance_tracker`, now what? Folded into one release because they
share a domain and complete the join loop end-to-end.

Item 1 — Admin inbox UI (templates/admin.html)
- New Orchestras tab in /admin. Filter by orchestra + status;
  Approve/Reject pending requests inline.
- Approve prompts for optional note; Reject requires a note
  (server enforces, UI blocks empty).
- Cards show finding_labels + multiplier_range summary plus a
  collapsible full proposed_contract JSON.
- Endpoints unchanged from v0.11.2 — pure frontend addition.

Item 2 — Counterfactual Brier substrate (football-manager model)
- New column fermi_forecasts.counterfactual_probability REAL,
  CHECK [0,1], via ensure_critical_schema (PgBouncer-safe).
- CreateForecastRequest.counterfactual_probability: Option<f64>,
  clamped defensively before insert.
- resolve_forecast_handler runs a best-effort UPDATE to compute
  counterfactual_brier = (cf_prob − outcome)² when populated.
  Failure does not roll back the resolve.
- GET /forecast and resolve response surface counterfactual_probability,
  counterfactual_brier, and manager_effect = brier − counterfactual_brier.
- Split of responsibility: client (Fermi harness) owns the naive-
  baseline formula and sends cf_prob at creation; server persists
  and computes the delta at resolution.

Item 3 — Dynamic roster injection into strategist system prompts
- New handlers::orchestras::inject_orchestra_context(db, card).
  Appends a `## CURRENT ROSTER` block listing live approved members
  from orchestra_*_members view when card.agent_id is a strategist.
- STRATEGIST_AGENTS = [("fermi", "orchestra_fermi_members")].
  xaman_ek intentionally deferred (100+ members = 4-5k tokens);
  waits on a compact digest view.
- Wired into both execute_agent_handler and
  execute_agent_stream_handler. Non-strategists pass through.
- Never fails: DB error logs and returns card unchanged. Empty
  roster skips injection.
- Solves the observed bug where Mario's approved guidance_tracker
  did not appear in Fermi's decompositions because the curated
  card hard-coded its original 4-specialist roster.

Migrations: none. Item 2 uses ensure_critical_schema.

